From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:07:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: duo.config: Qualcomm platform only

make defconfig enables every arm64 SoC platform; the Duo needs only ARCH_QCOM. With the 47 others off the kernel
image shrinks from 76.9 MiB to 54.5 MiB (image_size), under the ~60 MiB the phone's own bootloader (ABL) accepts,
and ~1460 other-vendor options go; every Duo-relevant option is unchanged. Tested on the phone: all drivers through
UEFI (duo-health: 0 failures), and booted directly by ABL with fastboot boot.

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/duo.config | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
index 90ea3a6d2..f053df9e1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/duo.config
@@ -433,3 +433,53 @@ CONFIG_USB_USBNET=y
 CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PCI_RENESAS=y
 CONFIG_VETH=y
 CONFIG_VIDEO_DW9719=m
+
